
# Lab 05 — PowerShell Network Troubleshooting

## Objective
Use PowerShell to inspect network configuration and test connectivity.

## Environment
- OS: Windows 11 Pro
- Account: BUTLERLAB\Administrator
- Tool: Windows PowerShell

## Procedures
1. Ran Get-NetIPConfiguration.
2. Reviewed IPv4 address, default gateway, and DNS server.
3. Ran Test-NetConnection google.com -Port 443.
4. Verified successful TCP connectivity.

## Findings
- Network configuration displayed successfully.
- Gateway and DNS information were present.
- TCP port 443 connectivity: True.

## Skills Practiced
- PowerShell network diagnostics.
- IP configuration inspection.
- DNS and connectivity troubleshooting.
- TCP port testing.

## Result
Successfully verified network configuration and HTTPS connectivity using PowerShell.
